\\begin{aligned}y>0 \\\\ {x}^{3}\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}y>0 \\\\ x\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>0,\\,x\\ne 0\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e365395e-e193-5723-b80a-2293c4ae62a0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e365395e-e193-5723-b80a-2293c4ae62a0" :answer-field/id #uuid "e365395e-e193-5723-b80a-2293c4ae62a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-94603c8a-00da-5e0e-8705-b52b7dbbcde4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-94603c8a-00da-5e0e-8705-b52b7dbbcde4" "answer-269efb88-268f-56aa-a516-6833ee078794" "answer-0c3c2367-c89a-5a63-909a-8ab545f01ec6" "answer-fa533f6d-4ad6-5d08-9dfd-22ac37f25112" "answer-d6a12713-af0d-576a-8ce3-2bf1f61336d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94603c8a-00da-5e0e-8705-b52b7dbbcde4" :answer/id #uuid "94603c8a-00da-5e0e-8705-b52b7dbbcde4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>0,\\,x\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-269efb88-268f-56aa-a516-6833ee078794" :answer/id #uuid "269efb88-268f-56aa-a516-6833ee078794" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c3c2367-c89a-5a63-909a-8ab545f01ec6" :answer/id #uuid "0c3c2367-c89a-5a63-909a-8ab545f01ec6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge 0,\\,x\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa533f6d-4ad6-5d08-9dfd-22ac37f25112" :answer/id #uuid "fa533f6d-4ad6-5d08-9dfd-22ac37f25112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ne 0,\\,x\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6a12713-af0d-576a-8ce3-2bf1f61336d5" :answer/id #uuid "d6a12713-af0d-576a-8ce3-2bf1f61336d5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e5fbae1b-fa0a-5638-bec4-5b64d04c9a07" :question/id #uuid "e5fbae1b-fa0a-5638-bec4-5b64d04c9a07" :question/math-academy-id "q-158185" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-y)}{{e}^{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nNotice that ${e}^{x}>0$ for all $x.$ Therefore, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y>0\\,⟹\\,x>y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x>y\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0495e322-ad63-52d2-84e8-e016c8d6367c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0495e322-ad63-52d2-84e8-e016c8d6367c" :answer-field/id #uuid "0495e322-ad63-52d2-84e8-e016c8d6367c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-809ffa9f-fc24-57db-8fe0-6f88da3c8f83" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b0f55a63-715f-589c-a5b9-f12320546593" "answer-809ffa9f-fc24-57db-8fe0-6f88da3c8f83" "answer-2e779e34-e7fe-559c-8a5e-d6acdf7c0dc0" "answer-90267910-6534-5e32-a7b2-2a165379570f" "answer-0c87b3c0-88bd-5bcd-8655-c1b7cc94de43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0f55a63-715f-589c-a5b9-f12320546593" :answer/id #uuid "b0f55a63-715f-589c-a5b9-f12320546593" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x>y,\\,x\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-809ffa9f-fc24-57db-8fe0-6f88da3c8f83" :answer/id #uuid "809ffa9f-fc24-57db-8fe0-6f88da3c8f83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x>y\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e779e34-e7fe-559c-8a5e-d6acdf7c0dc0" :answer/id #uuid "2e779e34-e7fe-559c-8a5e-d6acdf7c0dc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ne y,\\,x\\ne 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90267910-6534-5e32-a7b2-2a165379570f" :answer/id #uuid "90267910-6534-5e32-a7b2-2a165379570f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ne y\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c87b3c0-88bd-5bcd-8655-c1b7cc94de43" :answer/id #uuid "0c87b3c0-88bd-5bcd-8655-c1b7cc94de43" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8a09ec73-a8f5-5e32-98fd-165c3e60bda6" :question/id #uuid "8a09ec73-a8f5-5e32-98fd-165c3e60bda6" :question/math-academy-id "q-158183" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-y)}.$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y>0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-y)\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y>0 \\\\ x-y\\ne 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x-y>0,\\,x-y\\ne 1\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-421fe0aa-3a0a-5d77-af83-754300b22259"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-421fe0aa-3a0a-5d77-af83-754300b22259" :answer-field/id #uuid "421fe0aa-3a0a-5d77-af83-754300b22259" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b121cf1a-7dc7-5909-a04d-7262bf0ba8dd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b121cf1a-7dc7-5909-a04d-7262bf0ba8dd" "answer-c7eee758-44ec-5173-b8d7-7b012b545dcb" "answer-e9d25956-37d7-5565-be7f-161a70ab6752" "answer-d680f939-d4c5-5d9b-a170-a6f596fd8729" "answer-a3e6ed38-eb22-5a68-b4e4-a818bbc05c8c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b121cf1a-7dc7-5909-a04d-7262bf0ba8dd" :answer/id #uuid "b121cf1a-7dc7-5909-a04d-7262bf0ba8dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x-y>0,\\,x-y\\ne 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7eee758-44ec-5173-b8d7-7b012b545dcb" :answer/id #uuid "c7eee758-44ec-5173-b8d7-7b012b545dcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x-y>0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9d25956-37d7-5565-be7f-161a70ab6752" :answer/id #uuid "e9d25956-37d7-5565-be7f-161a70ab6752" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x-y\\ge 0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d680f939-d4c5-5d9b-a170-a6f596fd8729" :answer/id #uuid "d680f939-d4c5-5d9b-a170-a6f596fd8729" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x-y\\ne 0,1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3e6ed38-eb22-5a68-b4e4-a818bbc05c8c" :answer/id #uuid "a3e6ed38-eb22-5a68-b4e4-a818bbc05c8c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-aca8e51f-98b0-5cbe-9d48-2cf6165eb100" :question/id #uuid "aca8e51f-98b0-5cbe-9d48-2cf6165eb100" :question/math-academy-id "q-158194" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $g(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2})?$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n4-{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<4\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}<1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}<1\\}.\n$$\n\nSince the expression involves the $<$ sign, the curve is *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we draw the dashed curve $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}<1$ and shade the region *inside* the curve.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/59/59ac983361be7dd9a991e1cf134e7193256891a5587eab6bff5edf906fef3688.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d7edea41-50a3-50bd-89df-5921c02bca14"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d7edea41-50a3-50bd-89df-5921c02bca14" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7edea41-50a3-50bd-89df-5921c02bca14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-921a2c76-2d53-53a6-a4cc-08b4036be5ef" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5d3bfeec-8a70-54e7-b902-621589c010e6" "answer-873bd759-67ad-5785-b300-e95e0d07fa2c" "answer-2b746c30-aae0-5a72-8f59-c56e220b909e" "answer-48fd464b-717b-50cf-9914-97377d2a6891" "answer-921a2c76-2d53-53a6-a4cc-08b4036be5ef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d3bfeec-8a70-54e7-b902-621589c010e6" :answer/id #uuid "5d3bfeec-8a70-54e7-b902-621589c010e6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/5b/5b10601e98e7b8f4aea176c5a0eea21e806c61ecc8bf9e09bc231d36c848494b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-873bd759-67ad-5785-b300-e95e0d07fa2c" :answer/id #uuid "873bd759-67ad-5785-b300-e95e0d07fa2c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/7b/7b7973136f5add18c648db5589bab6e3f3a8f1f2544473274e37f28ab282b5d6.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b746c30-aae0-5a72-8f59-c56e220b909e" :answer/id #uuid "2b746c30-aae0-5a72-8f59-c56e220b909e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b1/b18e5383da3d9cd336d8829713127c670449da207ecc9216789747ee55ad3db7.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48fd464b-717b-50cf-9914-97377d2a6891" :answer/id #uuid "48fd464b-717b-50cf-9914-97377d2a6891" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/c1/c165cffbac8308d93d73db8323f2e89e6231f8661c0c010947861be46f0a0040.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-921a2c76-2d53-53a6-a4cc-08b4036be5ef" :answer/id #uuid "921a2c76-2d53-53a6-a4cc-08b4036be5ef" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/d6/d60f7727323089821783619f48be4d61146e463a5d694f0817276f0e8a0986b1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186378829 :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}+y\\ne 0\\,⟹\\,y\\ne -{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ne -{x}^{3}\\}.\n$$\n\nSince the expression involves the $\\ne $ sign, the line is *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we draw the dashed curve $y=-{x}^{3}$ and shade *above* and *below* the curve.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/6c/6c85783dc6626a3fea9d06431ee31e202da8c4d88e2eb1c2b6608dccdc2b782e.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186378746 :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\ny+{x}^{2}\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,y\\ge -{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge -{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves the $\\ge $ sign, the curve is part of the domain. Therefore, we draw a solid curve $y=-{x}^{2}$ and shade the area *outside* the curve.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/0b/0b7a6dbbab890b469cf389fa27627e9c1a5f95d8892507fcd4ba5f70541936ea.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-28327fac-a614-5756-91bd-3fcab54fcda2" :question/id #uuid "28327fac-a614-5756-91bd-3fcab54fcda2" :question/math-academy-id "q-158199" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $g(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x-y}}?$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\nx-y>0\\,⟹\\,y<x\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<x\\}.\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves the $>$ sign, the line is not part of the domain. Therefore, we draw a dashed line $y=x$ and shade the area *below* the line.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/77/77a1a03d037ee571fb0dc14ec8370c8b01f521b5a54798117c0b131000676599.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d3261e01-b350-524c-a353-a2dfc7e7e037"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d3261e01-b350-524c-a353-a2dfc7e7e037" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3261e01-b350-524c-a353-a2dfc7e7e037" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a52a1264-daf9-5585-a899-ca4955b26a0c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-24ee07ec-7db5-5819-9326-c35abfd13309" "answer-bb553729-44e6-50a1-8fbf-d734ae3b55c8" "answer-a52a1264-daf9-5585-a899-ca4955b26a0c" "answer-fae94e29-660b-5543-bab0-87e8d67f1ae2" "answer-b2b08043-54bd-579b-a710-49e36d027167"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24ee07ec-7db5-5819-9326-c35abfd13309" :answer/id #uuid "24ee07ec-7db5-5819-9326-c35abfd13309" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/02/02c770831bde33820dd4f616df872e22d1a1f9d2de4e49073043cbd4139408e4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb553729-44e6-50a1-8fbf-d734ae3b55c8" :answer/id #uuid "bb553729-44e6-50a1-8fbf-d734ae3b55c8" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/20/2058a5e83362c3a2b823169cab5044ea8c3756c6f99ad9f8d26234e9f3b4421d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a52a1264-daf9-5585-a899-ca4955b26a0c" :answer/id #uuid "a52a1264-daf9-5585-a899-ca4955b26a0c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/8f/8fc352405dfa98fc84dc5fc60a41d111139058b7680b9c3b02ee988079b34fef.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fae94e29-660b-5543-bab0-87e8d67f1ae2" :answer/id #uuid "fae94e29-660b-5543-bab0-87e8d67f1ae2" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/bb/bbf7c2cd4d8b11cd078f08d7ca31d3e7f40f20db3ee25fbbe95134d051840cc0.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2b08043-54bd-579b-a710-49e36d027167" :answer/id #uuid "b2b08043-54bd-579b-a710-49e36d027167" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ec/ec1f53deac4b4a4c29daf9ad8205b6283b09f9402ce4df20a46c47e268bcd374.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f90f5dc8-4e9d-5e87-800a-708d8b32cd8d" :question/id #uuid "f90f5dc8-4e9d-5e87-800a-708d8b32cd8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-158196" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $g(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}?$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1\\ge 0\n$$\n\nSince the inequality ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1\\ge 0$ is true for all values of $x$ and $y,$ the domain of the function $f$ is the entire $xy$-plane.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/40/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e1debb0e2463be408b489b.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b0c62e6a-7044-5e8e-b3aa-7123ad96f32d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b0c62e6a-7044-5e8e-b3aa-7123ad96f32d" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0c62e6a-7044-5e8e-b3aa-7123ad96f32d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fb69bb38-f4d8-5144-bff4-908369a1e63a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e69db1ea-c330-5536-8560-08f5b1e80164" "answer-fb69bb38-f4d8-5144-bff4-908369a1e63a" "answer-aeac4431-91c7-5505-8522-2946cd2d43cc" "answer-cdf6bb0c-4f48-5455-b7c2-33db2af70756" "answer-ff779dbe-e82e-5919-99da-f2d26cecb00a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e69db1ea-c330-5536-8560-08f5b1e80164" :answer/id #uuid "e69db1ea-c330-5536-8560-08f5b1e80164" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/33/338809ca0a3fe4d02c3523ec5e34a8d07a00b297d9f468740bbd1800d9675941.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb69bb38-f4d8-5144-bff4-908369a1e63a" :answer/id #uuid "fb69bb38-f4d8-5144-bff4-908369a1e63a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/40/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e1debb0e2463be408b489b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aeac4431-91c7-5505-8522-2946cd2d43cc" :answer/id #uuid "aeac4431-91c7-5505-8522-2946cd2d43cc" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/44/4453ab63ec12361c69cffbf76bd51d63a9ef985b54452f7f84e37ed7dee21c39.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdf6bb0c-4f48-5455-b7c2-33db2af70756" :answer/id #uuid "cdf6bb0c-4f48-5455-b7c2-33db2af70756" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/9c/9c2a0516ca58c52ccecadade60e966563b442f3112cce73cb16c1931c2087cd8.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff779dbe-e82e-5919-99da-f2d26cecb00a" :answer/id #uuid "ff779dbe-e82e-5919-99da-f2d26cecb00a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b8/b8fe923f727ca57a8a2cfc756b93c0ed522bdd9edcc06c8097bead979c8e4b15.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147575 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d64cbb84-4920-5e00-a5fb-dd325fcf710c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d64cbb84-4920-5e00-a5fb-dd325fcf710c" :question/id #uuid "d64cbb84-4920-5e00-a5fb-dd325fcf710c" :question/math-academy-id "q-60981" :question/problem "If $\\,\\boxed{}\\times 40%=32,$ then $\\,\\boxed{}=$" :question/worked-solution "The part is $32,$ the percentage is $40%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $40%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{40}{100}=\\frac{40÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =32÷40% \\\\  & =32÷\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =32\\times \\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{2}\\times 5 \\\\  & =16\\times 5 \\\\  & =80\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bcf715fb-fd7f-5fbf-bbe8-06f12ca3c63d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bcf715fb-fd7f-5fbf-bbe8-06f12ca3c63d" :answer-field/id #uuid "bcf715fb-fd7f-5fbf-bbe8-06f12ca3c63d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4fbab777-784f-5143-ac9a-4ea8efece70e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f43fb12c-ca5e-5bb9-a117-52a4220abfd0" "answer-7408b52e-5e63-584d-aca1-f327f1bffed4" "answer-99f37d1a-01b6-5eb6-896e-d89a1c5d9202" "answer-4fbab777-784f-5143-ac9a-4ea8efece70e" "answer-03e9cf25-ab69-52a6-934c-62bdcbd01856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f43fb12c-ca5e-5bb9-a117-52a4220abfd0" :answer/id #uuid "f43fb12c-ca5e-5bb9-a117-52a4220abfd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7408b52e-5e63-584d-aca1-f327f1bffed4" :answer/id #uuid "7408b52e-5e63-584d-aca1-f327f1bffed4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "68" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99f37d1a-01b6-5eb6-896e-d89a1c5d9202" :answer/id #uuid "99f37d1a-01b6-5eb6-896e-d89a1c5d9202" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "76" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fbab777-784f-5143-ac9a-4ea8efece70e" :answer/id #uuid "4fbab777-784f-5143-ac9a-4ea8efece70e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "80" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03e9cf25-ab69-52a6-934c-62bdcbd01856" :answer/id #uuid "03e9cf25-ab69-52a6-934c-62bdcbd01856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "84" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138830 :question/problem "![](images/a3/a3495fce9e81ae42fd279c91c964d7780daa1736c8a0c600dd2810a40f4ccbe8.png)\n\nGiven the diagram shown above, what is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "By the segment addition postulate, we have\n\n$$\nAD=AB+BC+CD.\n$$\n\nTo solve for $x,$ we can substitute the given information\n\n$$\nAD=17,\\,AB=x-2,\\,BC=9,\\,CD=2x-5,\n$$\n\n \n\nand then solve the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =AB+BC+CD \\\\ 17 & =(x-2)+9+(2x-5) \\\\ 17 & =3x+2 \\\\ 3x & =15 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135928 :answer-field/correct 17592186135929 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110630 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a1a77f56-694e-539a-a24b-49a13b3865ca"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a1a77f56-694e-539a-a24b-49a13b3865ca" :question/id #uuid "a1a77f56-694e-539a-a24b-49a13b3865ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-5926" :question/problem "![](images/c3/c3a31aad745cafe59f0c15e56dd48bf9350e46c08e148b843a6904145934e46b.png)\n\nSolve for $x$ given the figure above." :question/worked-solution "Since the two angles are supplementary, the sum of their measures is equal to ${180}^{∘}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{48}^{∘}+(x+{42}^{∘}) & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ x+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={90}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f15dd0ad-8bf1-5e1c-8d76-6465ccbd4d24"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f15dd0ad-8bf1-5e1c-8d76-6465ccbd4d24" :answer-field/id #uuid "f15dd0ad-8bf1-5e1c-8d76-6465ccbd4d24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-640dc449-205d-57f4-9327-7faa378ccea1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a3917857-9aaa-5c34-bf67-fac980d43439" "answer-42be2e85-427d-5ed0-b65f-e28375ab57c1" "answer-640dc449-205d-57f4-9327-7faa378ccea1" "answer-3f982969-e29b-5dcb-b520-dd0b13eb6833" "answer-c6250ade-5d8e-5049-bd28-9494165c15e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3917857-9aaa-5c34-bf67-fac980d43439" :answer/id #uuid "a3917857-9aaa-5c34-bf67-fac980d43439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{80}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42be2e85-427d-5ed0-b65f-e28375ab57c1" :answer/id #uuid "42be2e85-427d-5ed0-b65f-e28375ab57c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{87}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-640dc449-205d-57f4-9327-7faa378ccea1" :answer/id #uuid "640dc449-205d-57f4-9327-7faa378ccea1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f982969-e29b-5dcb-b520-dd0b13eb6833" :answer/id #uuid "3f982969-e29b-5dcb-b520-dd0b13eb6833" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{92}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6250ade-5d8e-5049-bd28-9494165c15e0" :answer/id #uuid "c6250ade-5d8e-5049-bd28-9494165c15e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{96}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129108 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3cdee882-c7e4-5094-92c4-9cde591d4ea6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3cdee882-c7e4-5094-92c4-9cde591d4ea6" :question/id #uuid "3cdee882-c7e4-5094-92c4-9cde591d4ea6" :question/math-academy-id "q-166673" :question/problem "![](images/34/34054404a184f9480abec1692e343f7ffbae4664c9c906e744f07cc082b0ebde.png)\n\nWhat are the roots of the function $f(x)$ defined by the mapping diagram shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The roots of the function are the values of $x$ such that $f(x)=0.$ In the given mapping diagram, we see that there is no value of $x$ that gives an output of zero. \n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ has no roots." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-73aaa492-1989-5edc-b375-a2b4ff1dbf0f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-73aaa492-1989-5edc-b375-a2b4ff1dbf0f" :answer-field/id #uuid "73aaa492-1989-5edc-b375-a2b4ff1dbf0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-491a4c71-5fdc-56c2-8fae-cd8a5438662b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bee91cba-2f60-53b4-8260-df36b392dd26" "answer-fa586a76-640b-54ff-9c72-afa240ba7b86" "answer-c323cd02-6f11-5b93-8f07-e4d3047852c5" "answer-fb462dfb-9442-515e-b89b-ef1366481882" "answer-491a4c71-5fdc-56c2-8fae-cd8a5438662b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bee91cba-2f60-53b4-8260-df36b392dd26" :answer/id #uuid "bee91cba-2f60-53b4-8260-df36b392dd26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa586a76-640b-54ff-9c72-afa240ba7b86" :answer/id #uuid "fa586a76-640b-54ff-9c72-afa240ba7b86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0$ and $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c323cd02-6f11-5b93-8f07-e4d3047852c5" :answer/id #uuid "c323cd02-6f11-5b93-8f07-e4d3047852c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0,1$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb462dfb-9442-515e-b89b-ef1366481882" :answer/id #uuid "fb462dfb-9442-515e-b89b-ef1366481882" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-491a4c71-5fdc-56c2-8fae-cd8a5438662b" :answer/id #uuid "491a4c71-5fdc-56c2-8fae-cd8a5438662b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ has no roots" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115311 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b024a1aa-681f-5f33-860b-bc65702c1e19"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b024a1aa-681f-5f33-860b-bc65702c1e19" :question/id #uuid "b024a1aa-681f-5f33-860b-bc65702c1e19" :question/math-academy-id "q-111439" :question/problem "Find all of the real solutions to the equation $(x-3)^{4}=-16.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $(x-3)^{4}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the exponent ($4$) is even. This expression can never be negative. \n\nTherefore, there are no real solutions to this equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ed337ad5-38b5-500f-9d10-ecd8816c9737"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ed337ad5-38b5-500f-9d10-ecd8816c9737" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed337ad5-38b5-500f-9d10-ecd8816c9737" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6ae61634-b5f8-59eb-a055-c867fddb17f2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7b92c85e-104a-5064-8305-943449567082" "answer-eb7d4e73-767a-50c3-bf1a-830bdd14c11f" "answer-2bed00fa-efb8-5c12-adfd-d23dd1427391" "answer-da4c22fc-fba0-5c21-9052-a20bc9a784c8" "answer-6ae61634-b5f8-59eb-a055-c867fddb17f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b92c85e-104a-5064-8305-943449567082" :answer/id #uuid "7b92c85e-104a-5064-8305-943449567082" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb7d4e73-767a-50c3-bf1a-830bdd14c11f" :answer/id #uuid "eb7d4e73-767a-50c3-bf1a-830bdd14c11f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bed00fa-efb8-5c12-adfd-d23dd1427391" :answer/id #uuid "2bed00fa-efb8-5c12-adfd-d23dd1427391" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-1$ and $7$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da4c22fc-fba0-5c21-9052-a20bc9a784c8" :answer/id #uuid "da4c22fc-fba0-5c21-9052-a20bc9a784c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$ and $5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ae61634-b5f8-59eb-a055-c867fddb17f2" :answer/id #uuid "6ae61634-b5f8-59eb-a055-c867fddb17f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no real solutions" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138414 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-dfc98e96-f028-5cd6-8e89-3ae59a19563f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-dfc98e96-f028-5cd6-8e89-3ae59a19563f" :question/id #uuid "dfc98e96-f028-5cd6-8e89-3ae59a19563f" :question/math-academy-id "q-115562" :question/problem "If $y$ varies inversely with $x$ and $y=2$ when $x=4,$ find the value of $y$ when $x=\\frac{4}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{k}{x}.\n$$\n\nWe are told that $y=2$ when $x=4.$ We substitute this data into the equation to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{k}{4} \\\\ 2\\cdot 4 & =k \\\\ 8 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the inverse variation is given by \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{8}{x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the value of $x=\\frac{4}{5}$ into this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{8}{(\\frac{4}{5})} \\\\  & =8÷\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{4} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-47ecb024-2722-561f-8432-d98acd72fb24"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-47ecb024-2722-561f-8432-d98acd72fb24" :answer-field/id #uuid "47ecb024-2722-561f-8432-d98acd72fb24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-27489401-06a5-55b9-b5cd-4c561edb32eb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-27489401-06a5-55b9-b5cd-4c561edb32eb" "answer-1e456658-a42b-5e79-b5ed-3a3fe1823913" "answer-aaf57b44-4131-58a8-9c32-4175e4939bf5" "answer-5f4845bc-6bd1-523b-9b3b-cd826c584ce3" "answer-3934a817-e1ce-57d9-a908-f6163578ca88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27489401-06a5-55b9-b5cd-4c561edb32eb" :answer/id #uuid "27489401-06a5-55b9-b5cd-4c561edb32eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e456658-a42b-5e79-b5ed-3a3fe1823913" :answer/id #uuid "1e456658-a42b-5e79-b5ed-3a3fe1823913" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aaf57b44-4131-58a8-9c32-4175e4939bf5" :answer/id #uuid "aaf57b44-4131-58a8-9c32-4175e4939bf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f4845bc-6bd1-523b-9b3b-cd826c584ce3" :answer/id #uuid "5f4845bc-6bd1-523b-9b3b-cd826c584ce3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3934a817-e1ce-57d9-a908-f6163578ca88" :answer/id #uuid "3934a817-e1ce-57d9-a908-f6163578ca88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175908 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e8061560-b60f-50e8-a1e6-e8fcd0b1f879"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e8061560-b60f-50e8-a1e6-e8fcd0b1f879" :question/id #uuid "e8061560-b60f-50e8-a1e6-e8fcd0b1f879" :question/math-academy-id "q-215145" :question/problem "Solve for $y$ where $-\\frac{1}{2y+7}=\\frac{4}{5y-2}.$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $y=-\\frac{7}{2}$ and $y=\\frac{2}{5}$ cannot be solutions since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nTo solve the equation, we move the negative sign onto the numerator of the fraction and then apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2y+7} & =\\frac{4}{5y-2} \\\\ \\frac{-1}{2y+7} & =\\frac{4}{5y-2} \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (5y-2) & =(2y+7)\\cdot 4 \\\\ -5y+2 & =8y+28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5y+2 & =8y+28 \\\\ -5y+2+5y & =8y+28+5y \\\\ 2 & =13y+28 \\\\ 2-28 & =13y+28-28 \\\\ -26 & =13y \\\\ \\frac{-26}{13} & =\\frac{13y}{13} \\\\ -2 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $y=-2$ is different from $y=-\\frac{7}{2}$ and $y=\\frac{2}{5},$ we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $y=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4382b096-445d-57f5-877e-794cba2c5eef"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4382b096-445d-57f5-877e-794cba2c5eef" :answer-field/id #uuid "4382b096-445d-57f5-877e-794cba2c5eef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-034dcf22-431a-57bb-93c4-4c3872d74663" :answer-field/choices ["answer-034dcf22-431a-57bb-93c4-4c3872d74663"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-034dcf22-431a-57bb-93c4-4c3872d74663" :answer/id #uuid "034dcf22-431a-57bb-93c4-4c3872d74663" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179631 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-01d6b59b-be2b-52a2-b7cf-129c1864b658"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-01d6b59b-be2b-52a2-b7cf-129c1864b658" :question/id #uuid "01d6b59b-be2b-52a2-b7cf-129c1864b658" :question/math-academy-id "q-128962" :question/problem "What is the slope of the line $4x-2y=15?$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the slope of the line if we can express its equation in slope-intercept form. To do this, we solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2y & =15 \\\\ -2y & =-4x+15 \\\\ 2y & =4x-15 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{2} & =\\frac{4x-15}{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x}{2}-\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ y & =2x-\\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the slope-intercept equation, we can tell that the slope of the line is $m=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ce1122d2-a474-5255-b4e6-fa64c2b26aea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ce1122d2-a474-5255-b4e6-fa64c2b26aea" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce1122d2-a474-5255-b4e6-fa64c2b26aea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-39431c77-c03d-5db8-a706-f5e48e50720a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3eb7519d-f9a4-537d-ad00-b8770df7304f" "answer-6a1392cc-72c9-552a-91a5-492a4e1eb7eb" "answer-39431c77-c03d-5db8-a706-f5e48e50720a" "answer-2919f4fb-39e3-5189-a03f-6a9b46e59de7" "answer-20d4b032-41eb-5439-8faf-8ee167214cea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3eb7519d-f9a4-537d-ad00-b8770df7304f" :answer/id #uuid "3eb7519d-f9a4-537d-ad00-b8770df7304f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a1392cc-72c9-552a-91a5-492a4e1eb7eb" :answer/id #uuid "6a1392cc-72c9-552a-91a5-492a4e1eb7eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39431c77-c03d-5db8-a706-f5e48e50720a" :answer/id #uuid "39431c77-c03d-5db8-a706-f5e48e50720a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2919f4fb-39e3-5189-a03f-6a9b46e59de7" :answer/id #uuid "2919f4fb-39e3-5189-a03f-6a9b46e59de7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20d4b032-41eb-5439-8faf-8ee167214cea" :answer/id #uuid "20d4b032-41eb-5439-8faf-8ee167214cea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147422 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d77788ff-b482-51d4-bdb1-79e3cff6db85"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d77788ff-b482-51d4-bdb1-79e3cff6db85" :question/id #uuid "d77788ff-b482-51d4-bdb1-79e3cff6db85" :question/math-academy-id "q-45552" :question/problem "A particular nature reserve started with $100$ rabbits. The number of rabbits is expected to increase sixfold each decade. What equation should we solve to determine the number of decades it will take for the rabbit population to increase to $129\\,600?$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the number of rabbits increases sixfold every decade. So the number of rabbits, which we'll call $y(t),$ grows exponentially with a growth factor of $6.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth factor $b$) is\n\n$$\ny(t)=a{b}^{t}.\n$$\n\nFrom the given information, we have the following:\n\n- $a=100$ is the initial number of rabbits.\n\n- $b=6$ is the growth factor.\n\n- $t$ is the time, in decades, since the opening of the nature reserve.\n\nTherefore, the expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\ny(t)=100\\cdot {6}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, to find the time it takes for the population to increase to $129\\,600,$ we would need to solve the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =129\\,600 \\\\ 100\\cdot {6}^{t} & =129\\,600.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b02529c2-774f-55c7-8d9d-1da2afa19817"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b02529c2-774f-55c7-8d9d-1da2afa19817" :answer-field/id #uuid "b02529c2-774f-55c7-8d9d-1da2afa19817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d42bbc30-223b-58ce-9507-9ce6ff98b241" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d42bbc30-223b-58ce-9507-9ce6ff98b241" "answer-85769fdc-2105-525f-b464-59ed6e084869" "answer-f005e8d6-8f28-556d-88bf-034ab9368e21" "answer-7c79c38a-0867-5379-a53c-7ca4269e7eef" "answer-b77e0798-376f-5ae6-bb3f-a714331eeca1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d42bbc30-223b-58ce-9507-9ce6ff98b241" :answer/id #uuid "d42bbc30-223b-58ce-9507-9ce6ff98b241" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100\\cdot {6}^{t}=129\\,600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85769fdc-2105-525f-b464-59ed6e084869" :answer/id #uuid "85769fdc-2105-525f-b464-59ed6e084869" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "129\\,600\\cdot {6}^{t}=100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f005e8d6-8f28-556d-88bf-034ab9368e21" :answer/id #uuid "f005e8d6-8f28-556d-88bf-034ab9368e21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\cdot {100}^{t}=129\\,600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c79c38a-0867-5379-a53c-7ca4269e7eef" :answer/id #uuid "7c79c38a-0867-5379-a53c-7ca4269e7eef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{100}^{t}=129\\,600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b77e0798-376f-5ae6-bb3f-a714331eeca1" :answer/id #uuid "b77e0798-376f-5ae6-bb3f-a714331eeca1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{6}^{t}=129\\,600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115408 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-78772149-6410-5606-9ad3-23c6e01f9b0e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-78772149-6410-5606-9ad3-23c6e01f9b0e" :question/id #uuid "78772149-6410-5606-9ad3-23c6e01f9b0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-117944" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f2dc2ed0562e3d93888ab025195ada5da5ef9bf5312d6215dfb83253c81f9be7.png)\n\nOrder the sides of $△KLM$ above from the shortest to the longest." :question/worked-solution "Since $∠K$ is the smallest angle, its opposite side $\\overset{―}{LM}$ is the shortest side of the triangle.\n\nSince $∠M$ is the largest angle, its opposite side $\\overset{―}{KL}$ must be the longest side of the triangle. \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nLM<KM<KL\n$$\n\nand therefore the required order is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{LM},\\,\\overset{―}{KM},\\,\\overset{―}{KL}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0164330c-13ad-5c34-8a92-9c663242c3e8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0164330c-13ad-5c34-8a92-9c663242c3e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "0164330c-13ad-5c34-8a92-9c663242c3e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-fi